James reported issues with his solar installation from Green Home Systems, including difficulties receiving responses after sending a registered letter that was returned. I advised him to act in parallel by re-sending the letter to the new forwarding address and any other addresses in his contract. I suggested checking the Minnesota Secretary of State records for the company's registered agent and emphasized the importance of sending communications via certified mail and email. I also recommended consulting a Minnesota construction/contract lawyer due to the delay, to navigate potential next steps such as termination or payment disputes. Caution was advised against signing any documents related to cancellation or changes without legal review, emphasizing the value of his previous communications as evidence of good faith efforts.
